claimed: okay-script-site -- okay-script as a JSP-level web framework (operator ask 2026-09-06, scope 'everything at once'). A directory of .md pages served over okay-http/okay-jetty: Site(root).routes: PartialFunction[Request, Response ! Async] (path -> page.md, index.md, [param].md, static files); okay.script.api package DELEGATED to the host classloader (servlet-API style; everything else stays isolated) so Web (now with form/cookies/body/params), Response (status/headers/contentType/redirect/cookie), Session (cookie-backed, TTL), include/forward cross the classloader boundary as ONE class identity -- Web.encodeArgs/decodeArgs go away; ```scala declare blocks emitted at object level (JSP <%! %>); error page (error.md / front-matter errorPage) on compile error or throw; contentType front-matter. Touches build.sbt (okayScript gains okayHttp.jvm as a MAIN dependency; okayJetty stays Test-only), moves okay.script.Web to okay.script.api.Web, edits ScalaScript.compileOnly's loader + Page. Live tests bind a real Jetty port.
